Z||000000||BlackARROW||09-26-2001||01:52 PM||||I have been wondering for a long while:<P>Did they make Stock Fiero T-Top model?  I have seen a lot of Fiero, and all of them had the sunroof (except one I saw with no sunroof - I thought he had modified it to have a closed top). I saw the posts telling how to do it, but was wondering  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Do you know if they made Targa-type top too?  I think it would kick ash  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR>BA-&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||09-26-2001||01:56 PM||||T tops were available in some pre 88 years as a dealer option and in 88 as a factory option, the sunroof was a factory option from day one. The hole for the sunroof in the spaceframe is on all Fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero_hunter85||09-26-2001||01:57 PM||||some of the 88 fiero's came with factory t-tops. some fiero's from 84-88 came without a sunroof too. i dont think they made a targa top fiero but i wish they did.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Kasdan||09-26-2001||10:13 PM||||Solid roof standard, although a majority have a sunroof.  i think t-tops were a dealer option starting in 86, and factory opt in 88<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">         <BR>Power Steering, Holley Scoop<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
